content:
For the waiver removal reckoning of Term Life Insurance — the reckoning of the installment after the waiver of premium rider ends — the band factor applied to the face premium is read from the band measurement face on one of two ladders. The renewable ladder applies to the Ashgrove Annual Renewable Term and to any term policy past its level premium period; the level term ladder applies to a level term policy within its level premium period (a level term policy is past that period once the whole months from its issue date to today reach twelve times its premium guarantee period in years).

**Ladder.**

- band measurement face of 1000000 or more: 0.74 on the level term ladder, 0.82 on the renewable ladder;
- from 500000 up to 1000000: 0.80 on the level term ladder, 0.86 on the renewable ladder;
- from 250000 up to 500000: 0.88 on the level term ladder, 0.92 on the renewable ladder;
- below 250000: 1.00 on either ladder.

**Both sides of each threshold (hypothetical, level term ladder):** 999999 gives 0.80 and 1000000 gives 0.74; 499999 gives 0.88 and 500000 gives 0.80; 249999 gives 1.00 and 250000 gives 0.88.

**Ladder choice (hypothetical):** an Ashgrove Level Term 15 in its 16th policy year (more than 180 whole months since issue) with a band measurement face of 550000 takes 0.86 from the renewable ladder; in its 12th policy year it takes 0.80 from the level term ladder. An Ashgrove Annual Renewable Term always reads the renewable ladder.

Figure, hypothetical: face on record 400000 at a rate per 1,000 of 2.50 with a factor of 0.88 gives a face premium of 400 times 2.50 times 0.88, which is 880.00.
